  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fostering freedom of expression and safety of journalists in Eastern Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Nairobi Regional Office for Eastern Africa will raise awareness and enhance the capacities of Member States, duty-bearers and rights holders on freedom of expression and access to information, in line with C/5 Output 5.1. Activities include supporting national and regional commemorations including the World Press Freedom Day (WPFD), the International Day for Universal Access to Information (IDUAI), and World Radio Day; strengthening the capacities of key duty-bearers and rights holders through training and advocacy; supporting Member States in developing and strengthening legal and policy frameworks on access to information; and providing expert advice on the governance of digital platforms in line with UNESCO&#x2019;s Guidelines for the Governance of Digital Platforms. USD 10,000 is delegated to the UNESCO Office in Tanzania.</narrative>
  </description>
